  "note": "Stage 4 checksum: every non-transient field of every saveable entity, via stateKeys(). The Stage 0 numbers (7d6b6b04 / 73a0cc05 / 3431063b) held unchanged through Stages 1-3 and are NOT comparable with these — the widening is what ended that comparability, and it was done in a commit of its own so the discontinuity has exactly one cause. snapshots.*.state carries the entity and field counts beside the hash, so a drift says how much moved as well as that something did. Regenerated once in Stage 5: tagging `base-trade-rate-research` as `ResearchTradeRate` changed that entity`s id prefix, since ids key on the tag. Verified to be the only difference by normalising ids out of both DTO dumps and comparing — `_` still reports `Research`, so nothing the renderer reads moved. Regenerated again in Stage 6: `Rule` gained an `_id` field, and a rule is reachable through `Unit._busy`, so `_id: null` now appears in the DTO for every fortified unit. Turn 1 is unchanged because nothing is fortified yet. That leak is what fixing `_busy` removes, which will move these numbers once more and shrink them. Since then it has been regenerated whenever a change was meant to alter play (each such PR says so). #253 widened it again, in a commit of its own: the city builds and city growth registries are now hashed too, so all three checkpoints moved with play unchanged. #194 then changed play (Auto, and computer players choosing improvements by need), regenerated in the lockfile commit that brought it in, and #378 again (computer players ranking units with improvements and Wonders), likewise, as did #30 (the Great Wall and the United Nations keeping other leaders peaceful towards their owner), #31 (the terrain, City Walls and fortified defence bonuses of Civ1 in combat), #115 with #236 (Isaac Newton's College and Hoover Dam taking effect, Michelangelo's Chapel and J.S. Bach's Cathedral as in v474.05), and #241 with #380 (buy prices as in v474.05, and no unit purchases in civil disorder: one Spend rule fewer, and the prices in the DTO change, but play does not). #31 (selling an improvement: a Sell and a Sold rule more, and each improvement's saleValue in the DTO) changes no play, though turn 50's state hash moves: the sale values built for the turn-10 DTO take ids, so entities created after it are numbered differently. Random calls and entity and field counts are unchanged. #459 shrinks the DTO: a player's units no longer include its destroyed ones. Play does not change.",
